    "final_answer": "I have found the answer. The page at https://info.arxiv.org/help/withdraw.html provides clear instructions on withdrawing an article that has not yet been announced.\n\n## Answer\n\nAccording to the ArXiv Help page on **Withdraw / Retract a Submission**, if your submission has **not yet been announced** (i.e., not yet publicly available), you have two options to effectively withdraw it:\n\n### Instructions for a submission not yet announced:\n\n1. **Go to your user page** on arXiv.\n\n2. **Select one of the two icons** next to the submission:\n   - **Delete icon (🗑️)** – This will **remove the submission entirely** from the arXiv system.\n   - **Unsubmit icon (↩️)** – This will **return the submission to \"incomplete\" status**, allowing you to modify it and resubmit later.\n\n3. **If you have difficulty** performing either of these actions, **contact arXiv administrators immediately**. In your message, include:\n   - The submission identifier\n   - An explanation of the problem\n   - The reason for withdrawal\n\n### Key Difference (announced vs. not announced):\n- **Not yet announced**: You can simply **delete** or **unsubmit** the paper (no public trace remains).\n- **Already announced**: The article cannot be fully removed. A withdrawal creates a **new version** marked as withdrawn, with the reason displayed publicly, but **previous versions remain accessible** including the full text.\n\nSource: https://info.arxiv.org/help/withdraw.html",
